docs {
  A linkset for a party-role GLN (AI 413, ship-for), so GS1's resolver test
  suite can be run against one of the five keys that became resolvable with
  PartyRoleGlnValidator.

  WHY 413 AND NOT ALL FIVE

  410, 411, 412, 413 and 415 share one validator — the same 13-digit GLN as
  414 and 417, only the AI and the role name in the message differ. One record
  therefore proves the path for all five. 413 is picked because it was the
  awkward case: it was declared in the resolver's AI enum and advertised in
  supportedPrimaryKeys, but had no validator, so it was refused like an
  invented AI while being listed as supported. That mismatch is exactly what
  the field exists to prevent.

  NOT 416

  Deliberately no record for 416 (production/service location). GS1's
  description-file schema does not admit it in supportedPrimaryKeys at all,
  the resolver refuses it, and a test record would suggest otherwise.

  AFTER CREATING IT

  Run https://ref.gs1.org/test-suites/resolver/ against
  {{dl-url}}/413/9521890340331 — expected 60/60 as for the GTIN.
}
